From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:05:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 029/159] [ae-patch] Add keep_runs to scheduled tasks and a
 post-fire observer seam

Every firing of a scheduled task starts a new session and nothing removes
the old ones: the two weekday AE tasks leave about ten sessions a week in
the sidebar. Reid decided on 2026-10-13 to keep each task's newest N run
sessions (default 5) and delete older ones after each firing.

This patch is the mechanism; what to delete is decided by an observer the
AE layer registers (ae_omni_policies.retention), so without one the server
keeps every session as before.

- keep_runs on ScheduledTask and on /v1/scheduled-tasks create, patch,
  get and list (1 to 1000, null keeps every run session), plus the
  sys_scheduled_task_create/update tool schemas and dispatch allowlists.
  It lives in its own table, ae_scheduled_task_retention, created on first
  use, so no Alembic revision is needed; a task never set reads 5.
- omnigent/server/scheduled/retention.py (new): the setting, the fire
  observer registry (awaited after a fire is created, granted, launched and
  recorded, inside the fire's background task so the per-task in-flight
  guard covers it; errors are logged, never raised), and
  delete_session_server_side, the server-owned part of
  DELETE /v1/sessions/{id} for a caller with no request. It refuses a
  session with a git worktree.
- fire.py gains two lines (import and call); the routes file resolves and
  stores the setting beside each existing store call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
